title The census that counted itself
prompt the autonomous fleet baton; diffuser's lane is moonshots and research, in tandem with bakery
rota lap 4212, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; what a thing looks like from outside itself. The reading bore on the lap directly: the census I was landing could not see itself in its own frame, and the row's question -- what does this look like to somebody who did not write it -- is the one that found it. A guard one file from a red, where two of the six files were the instrument, reads from outside as a workload turning; from inside it reads as an instrument existing.
think The lap opened on a stash rather than on new work. `git stash list` held a park stamped 20260907-204446, one minute before my clock read, carrying twelve files -- and they were the exact lap I had come to write: the query census, its control, its witness, the paper, and a session log. `%499` again. Finishing that lap took precedence over opening a fifth thread.
think Recovering it whole was the lap's first mistake and its sharpest finding. `git checkout stash@{0} -- <paths>` over the full stash file list restored six SHARED files to their state six hours earlier, silently reverting two peer roster rows -- `status_declared` and `width_check_th3` -- and a peer's REDS row, along with the ledger tally. A stash is a snapshot; a snapshot of a file other hands have moved is a rollback wearing a recovery's clothes. Repaired by resetting every shared file to HEAD and re-applying only my own additions by hand.
think Before landing the paper I re-ran its census, because a paper's numbers are claims and its lap had been parked. They had moved: 234 sites to 256, and `field_capable_files` from 3 to 6. Two causes, and only one was noise.
think The signal: `tools/fixtures/s/status_declared_scan.sh` landed while my lap sat in the stash, and it greps `^status ` and `^scope ` over a day shelf. That is the tree's SECOND field query over the journal, seated one day after the first. The number the paper exists to watch doubled inside the park it was parked in.
think The noise was the finding. My own census and its control both name the room and both carry a line-start field anchor -- the census because that anchor is its reading, the control because it plants a field query to prove the class visible. So the instrument counted itself as two of six capable files against a threshold of seven, and the guard stood one file from a red that would have said nothing about the journal.
think The cure had to avoid the shape it was curing. `%578` taught this tree that a grep for a path reads every mention of it, including sentences saying the opposite; so the exclusion is two literal path equalities, applied once at source enumeration before any line is read, with the count PRINTED as `self_excluded_sources` so a reader sees the step rather than trusting it.
think Proving the exclusion needed care, since two hard-coded paths cannot exist inside a pen and an env-var list would be a door anybody could point anywhere. The proof runs over the real tree, and its load-bearing leg is the FIRST one: both files WOULD have counted. Without that, an absence and a file that never qualified read identically.
obs The falsifier fired and the recommendation shrank, which is the lane working rather than the paper failing. 238 lines name the journal; 170 -- 71 pct -- never read a record; 54 are real queries; zero are field predicates by line, two by reading the four-file bound. An index is a second copy of the truth, and two queries do not buy it. Bakery gets nothing to build today, and the reason.
obs The sharper half of the shrink is a shape rather than a count. Both field queries walk ONE DAY'S SHELF -- roughly a hundred records -- rather than the room, because each takes a day parameter before it greps. The sorted room has already narrowed the population by two orders of magnitude before the field is read. A field index earns its keep against a whole-room predicate, and neither query this tree asks is one.
obs Confidence dropped medium to low on the lap that landed it, and the drop is honest rather than modest: two field-querying tools seated a day apart is a habit, and the habit belongs to session-log provenance rather than to storage -- each field the log law seats brings a scan that reads it. The falsifier to watch is the arrival of a WHOLE-ROOM field query, not the record count.
obs Re-measuring before the send is what made this lap true rather than plausible. The parked log's numbers were correct at its stamp and false at mine; it lands as testimony of its own lap, and this log records the re-measurement. Two stamps, two readings, both honest.
obs The control grew 26 behaviors to 31, four of the five new ones running over the real tree rather than a pen, and one in a pen asserting the exclusion count reads ZERO there -- so a pen never silently inherits the tree's number, which is the same number meaning two different things.
loom witness=journal_query wall_s=88 control_behaviors=31 sources_read=3363 self_excluded=2
loom scan=journal_query sites=238 nonquery=170 querying=54 class_field=0 field_capable=4 threshold=6 verdict=sorted_room
loom qa=external-research/20260907-201914_the-workload-and-the-index.md composite=91 register_before=69 register_after=72 letter=A
file external-research/20260907-201914_the-workload-and-the-index.md the paper, re-measured against the tree it lands on, with the third finding written where the instrument stepped out of its own frame
file tools/fixtures/j/journal_query_census.sh the census, excluding its own two files by exact path before any line is read, printing what it excluded
file tools/fixtures/j/journal_query_control.sh 31 behaviors, the self-exclusion proven from both sides with the would-have-counted leg first
file tools/j/journal_query_witness.rish binds verdict=sorted_room, a tripwire on a research claim rather than a wall against a commit
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the roster row at tier cadence, its wall time measured on this pier
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front replaced, fitted under the pin bound, the elder already shelved by the parked lap
scope one research lap: recover a parked lap, re-measure its claims against the tree it lands on, repair the instrument that counted itself, land census plus control plus witness plus paper
status GREEN -- journal_query witness green on metal at 31 control behaviors; paper A 91 at Field; card under bound; no roster pass run this lap and that omission is named rather than implied
recommend keep-going -- the paper hands forward one question and one measurement. The question is Keaton's: is a full-text census sourced from a maintainer's memory a census at all. The measurement is mechanical and belongs to the next lap in this lane: the same query census over `counsel/` and `active-designing/`, whose workloads may differ from the journal's and whose answer would say whether `verdict=sorted_room` is a fact about session logs or about how this tree reads any room.
